Aim:-
Write a program to implement control flow statement in python

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Input runs_scored, balls_faced, wickets_taken, runs_conceded, overs_bowled, catches_taken
3. Calculate Strike Rate
   strike_rate = (runs_scored / balls_faced) × 100
4. Calculate Economy Rate
   economy_rate = runs_conceded / overs_bowled
5. Check Batting Performance
   If runs_scored ≥ 50 and strike_rate ≥ 120 → batter = "excellent batter"
   Else if runs_scored ≥ 30 and strike_rate ≥ 100 → batter = "good batter"
   Else if runs_scored ≥ 20 → batter = "average batter"
   Else → batter = "poor batter"
6. Check Bowling Performance
   If wickets_taken ≥ 3 and economy_rate ≤ 6 → bowler = "excellent bowler"
   Else if wickets_taken ≥ 2 and economy_rate ≤ 8 → bowler = "good bowler"
   Else if wickets_taken ≥ 1 → bowler = "average bowler"
   Else → bowler = "poor bowler"
7. Check Fielding Performance
   If catches_taken ≥ 2 → fielder = "outstanding fielder"
   Else if catches_taken = 1 → fielder = "active fielder"
   Else → fielder = "needs improvement"
8. Determine Overall Result
   If batter = "excellent batter" and bowler = "excellent bowler" → result = "Star all-rounder"
   Else if batter = "good batter" and bowler = "good bowler" → result = "Strong all-rounder"
   Else if batter = "good batter" and bowler = "poor bowler" → result = "Supporting all-rounder"
   Else → result = "needs improvement"
9. Display strike_rate, economy_rate, batter, bowler, fielder, result
10. Stop

Code:-
runs_scored = int(input("Enter runs scored: "))
balls_faced = int(input("Enter balls faced: "))
wickets_taken = int(input("Enter wickets taken: "))
runs_conceded = int(input("Enter runs conceded: "))
overs_bowled = float(input("Enter overs bowled: "))
catches_taken = int(input("Enter catches taken: "))

strike_rate = (runs_scored / balls_faced) * 100 
economy_rate = runs_conceded / overs_bowled 

if runs_scored >= 50 and strike_rate >= 120:
    batter = "excellent batter"
elif runs_scored >= 30 and strike_rate >= 100:
    batter = "good batter"
elif runs_scored >= 20:
    batter = "average batter"
else:
    batter = "poor batter"

if wickets_taken >= 3 and economy_rate <= 6:
    bowler = "excellent bowler"
elif wickets_taken >= 2 and economy_rate <= 8:
    bowler = "good bowler"
elif wickets_taken >= 1:
    bowler = "average bowler"
else:
    bowler = "poor bowler"

if catches_taken >= 2:
    fielder = "outstanding fielder"
elif catches_taken == 1:
    fielder = "active fielder"
else:
    fielder = "needs improvement"

if batter == "excellent batter" and bowler == "excellent bowler":
    result = "Star all-rounder"
elif batter == "good batter" and bowler == "good bowler":
    result = "Strong all-rounder"
elif batter == "good batter" and bowler == "poor bowler":
    result = "Supporting all-rounder"
else:
    result = "needs improvement"

print("Strike rate:", strike_rate)
print("Economy rate:", economy_rate)
print("Batting:", batter)
print("Bowling:", bowler)
print("Fielding:", fielder)
print("Overall result:", result)

Output:-
Enter runs scored: 100
Enter balls faced: 50
Enter wickets taken: 5
Enter runs conceded: 20
Enter overs bowled: 4
Enter catches taken: 5
Strike rate: 200.0
Economy rate: 5.0
Batting: excellent batter
Bowling: excellent bowler
Fielding: outstanding fielder
Overall result: Star all-rounder


Aim:-
